**My overall assessment:** the project has made meaningful progress, particularly in the Python miner and the underlying governance architecture. But the most important remaining work is not adding more engines or visual features. It is closing the boundary between *a declared capability* and *a demonstrated capability*.

The new evidence gate is the right correction. I would make it mandatory across all three codebases, with no Phase 5 approval until the real-registry-to-atomic-admission path has been executed and independently verified.

